-- title:
--   Joint descent of ̄ K-points to a finite complete DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero, and write $\bar K$ for `AlgebraicClosure (FractionRing 𝒪)`. Let $A$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra that is finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, and let $\chi : A \to \bar K$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism. Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $S'$ a set of natural numbers, and let [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S'$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$ with $q \notin S'$. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from this Hecke algebra to $\mathbb C$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image subring $\chi_g(\mathbb T)$ into $\bar K$. The assertion is that there exist a type $\mathcal O'$ carrying the structure of a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure making $\mathcal O'$ finite as an $\mathcal O$-module and $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O'$ a local homomorphism, and maps $j : \mathcal O' \to \bar K$ and $\psi : A \to \mathcal O'$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras and a ring homomorphism $\iota' : \chi_g(\mathbb T) \to \mathcal O'$, such that $j$ is injective, $j(\psi(a)) = \chi(a)$ for all $a \in A$, and $j(\iota'(z)) = \iota(z)$ for all $z \in \chi_g(\mathbb T)$.
--
--   This is the standard coefficient-ring descent step: a $\bar K$-valued point of a module-finite $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with a $\bar K$-valued realisation of a Hecke eigencharacter, factors through a single finite extension $\mathcal O'$ of $\mathcal O$ which is again a complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field. It is used in the analysis of points of the local Hecke algebra with values in discrete valuation rings, namely by the computations of sums of residual root multiplicities at ordinary and non-ordinary primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeAlgebra_exists_dvr_algHom_comp_eq_and_ringHom_comp_eq_of_algHom_algebraicClosure.lean

